<h1>Connectors</h1>
<p>A <strong>connector</strong> is a pre-built integration to an external system that a <code>Pipeline</code> reads from or writes to. Connectors handle authentication, batching, and retry behavior for a specific system so pipeline authors don't have to.</p>

<h2>Connector direction</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Source</strong> — emits events into a pipeline (e.g. a change-data-capture stream from Postgres).</li>
  <li><strong>Destination</strong> — receives events from a pipeline (e.g. writing rows into Snowflake).</li>
  <li><strong>Bidirectional</strong> — a small set of connectors, like the generic Webhook connector, can act as either.</li>
</ul>

